Comment: I have tried that solution but it is not working.

Comment: You should share your code that you have tried and the error you are getting.

Answer: If you want to remove all duplicates from the array, then you can use [`array_unique`](http://php.net/manual/en/function.array-unique.php)

\begin{code}
$arr = array('test', 'test');
$uniqueArray = array_unique($arr);
\end{code}

If you want to remove only the first occurrence of the duplicate, then you can use [`array_search`](http://php.net/manual/en/function.array-search.php) to get the key of the duplicate and remove it using [`array_splice`](http://php.net/manual/en/function.array-splice.php)

\begin{code}
$arr = array('test', 'test');
$key = array_search('test', $arr);
if ($key!== false) {
    array_splice($arr, $key, 1);
}
\end{code}

Answer: This will remove the first occurrence of the duplicate value.

\begin{code}
$arr = array('test', 'test');
foreach ($arr as $key => $val) {
    if (array_search($val, $arr)!== $key) {
        unset($arr[$key]);
    }
}
\end{code}

